      "card_ids": ["C137","C179","C149","C164"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 oral exposure records for trimetazidine, a trimethoxybenzene basic amine, show substantial systemic exposure after oral modified-release tablets (Cmax 79–153 ng/mL; AUCinf 1838–2505 ng·h/mL), consistent with meaningful oral absorption in humans.",
      "card_ids": ["C87","C92","C99","C112","C119","C120"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L1 human F values for close basic methoxyaryl amine analogues remain above 20%: alizapride 72.5% (C04, C20, C30), vernakalant 40.2–81.8% by metabolizer phenotype (C09, C23, C54, C66), daridorexant 62% (C07, C10, C16, C19, C22), and encainide in cirrhosis 48–105% (C08, C17, C29, C59, C63, C78).",
      "card_ids": ["C04","C20","C30","C09","C23","C54","C66","C07","C10","C16","C19","C22","C08","C17","C29","C59","C63","C78"]
